{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqe5s77kk7e","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"[ingest-candidate] touchAgent fix requires uncommitted audit-sprint prerequisite files to have any effect","summary":"source_task=091a4bf1-b671-4ff9-854d-993775faa5ee/20\nwhy: The touchAgent one-field fix (persisting agent_tool_spawn) is silently inert without two other files from the uncommitted audit-sprint tree — without them the fix exists in code but the gate path that reads the field never runs.\nArm (b) of the overlay claim gate (routes/overlay.js: `a.agent_tool_spawn && a.agent_id === b.agent_id`) and agentToolSpawn detection (routes/exec.js) are NOT committed to main as of base commit 8232b19. The touchAgent fix is meaningless without them — arm (b) can never match because the field is never set in exec.js. Workers verified this by importing both prerequisite files into the worktree to make the branch self-consistent. Any deployment that applies only the touchAgent patch without the overlay.js + exec.js counterparts will still reject all Agent-tool subagent claims.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-14T19:09:51.104Z","vec":[-0.05970145761966705,0.0021756093483418226,0.028275376185774803,0.020863864570856094,0.0924447625875473,-0.09702475368976593,0.029475072398781776,-0.01397374551743269,0.007206467445939779,0.05974942818284035,0.0643145814538002,-0.02025241032242775,-0.011929884552955627,0.027069630101323128,-0.002876393496990204,0.02313770167529583,0.020122645422816277,-0.04839390888810158,-0.009913692250847816,0.00799121055752039,-0.017026955261826515,0.004796044435352087,0.07842143625020981,-0.04577816650271416,-0.04516766592860222,-0.07624427229166031,-0.12564103305339813,-0.03203628212213516,-0.022646887227892876,-0.08020615577697754,0.040154773741960526,0.1463737040758133,-0.07605043798685074,-0.04148096591234207,0.08339909464120865,0.12028709799051285,-0.02334502525627613,-0.025171855464577675,-0.019090943038463593,0.03398890048265457,0.0579298399